  "body": "A Mission Bay address, less than 300 metres from the beach, with the opportunity to make it your own.\r\n\r\nHere's your chance to secure a home in one of Auckland's most sought-after Eastern Bays locations, where morning swims, waterfront cafés, restaurants, shops and beautiful coastal walks are all just a short stroll away. And with offers over $1,295,000, this is an opportunity worth exploring!\r\n\r\nTucked away from the hustle and bustle of the waterfront, 7D Atkin Avenue offers a surprisingly peaceful setting, with everything that makes Mission Bay so desirable right on your doorstep.\r\n\r\nLive in it. Rent it out. Renovate when you're ready.\r\n\r\nWith nearly 130sqm of floor space, this Mission Bay home offers the flexibility to move in and enjoy it as it is, rent it out or modernise and add value over time. There's no need to do everything at once. Secure the location now and make it your own when you're ready.\r\n\r\nWhether you're a family looking for a home in the Kohimarama School and Selwyn College zones, a busy professional seeking a convenient coastal lifestyle, a downsizer wanting to enjoy the Eastern Bays or an astute investor looking for rental potential and future renovation opportunities, this property deserves your attention.\r\n\r\nThe Location. The Lifestyle. The Numbers.\r\n\r\n*  CV: $1,650,000\r\n\r\n*  Floor area: 127sqm\r\n\r\n*  Rental appraisal: $950-$980 per week\r\n\r\n*  Council rates 2026/2027: $5,319.26\r\n\r\n*  School zones: Kohimarama School and Selwyn College\r\n\r\n*  Location: Less than 300 metres from Mission Bay Beach\r\n\r\nOur vendors are committed to selling this year.\r\n\r\nWith summer just around the corner, why wait? This could be your opportunity to settle in and enjoy the best of Mission Bay over the warmer months.\r\n\r\nDon't judge this opportunity from the photos alone. Come and see the location, the lifestyle and the potential for yourself.\r\n\r\nDEADLINE SALE: Closes 2:00pm, Wednesday 2 December 2026 (Unless Sold Prior).\r\n\r\nContact Angelina Vihrova on 021 727 751 or Jacqueline McGearty 021 283 2033 to arrange a private viewing, or we look forward to seeing you at the open home.\r\n\r\n* Please note that photos with staging are virtually staged.",
